<title>USA: United Stationers CEO Sturgess resigns.</title>
<headline>United Stationers CEO Sturgess resigns.</headline>
<dateline>DES PLAINES, Ill. 1996-11-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>United Stationers Inc said on Monday that Thomas Sturgess has resigned as chairman, president and chief executive.</p>
<p>The company said he resigned to spend more time with his family.</p>
<p>Frederick Hegi Jr., currently chairman of the executive committee of the board, will assume the role of chairman, president and chief executive on an interim basis, the company said.</p>
<p>Sturgess will continue as a director.</p>
</text>
